course: dictionary
lesson: 13755
title: Formal words at funerals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. They sound serious and grown-up, and people use them in special places. Interment is one of these words. It means the burying of a dead person's body in a grave or tomb.
explain: «The interment will follow the service.» At a funeral, the service comes first, and the clue is that the next thing is the burial. So interment must mean burial. Check it by swapping in burial: «The burial will follow the service» still makes sense.
explain: You will meet interment in newspapers, church notices and old stories. It tells you that someone has died and is being laid to rest with respect. When you see a formal word, look for the clues around it, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Interment means the burying of a dead person's body in a grave or tomb.
fact: An interment is one burial, the ceremony when a body is laid in the ground.
fact: Interment is a formal word, so it is used at funerals, in church notices and in newspapers.
fact: «Interment will follow» means the burial will happen next.
fact: «Place of interment» means the place where the burial happens.
exercise: «The interment will take place in the village churchyard on Tuesday.» What does interment mean here? | *The burial of the body in the ground | A party to celebrate a birthday | A long walk to the church | A new church bell
exercise: «Only the family came to the private interment.» What does private tell us? | It was a happy party with music | Anyone in the town could come and join in | *Only a few close people were invited | It was held at a school sports day
exercise: Ella reads a church notice: «Interment will follow the service.» What happens next? | A school trip | A dinner in the hall | *The burial | The start of a football match
test: Which simple word means much the same as interment? | *Burial | Sunshine | Hallway | Holiday
test: «The king's tomb was opened for the interment of his son.» What does interment mean in this sentence? | Cleaning the stone steps | Painting the tomb white | *The burial of his son in the tomb | Opening the castle door
exam: Which sentence uses interment correctly? | Her interment is my favourite colour. | I had an interment of cheese for lunch. | Shall we go to the park for an interment? | *The family gathered for the interment at the cemetery.
